  I knew he would be able to adapt George  RR Martin's novel with a certain amount  of accuracy and with Miguel working  alongside him I knew he would be able to  help bring it to life on the screen  better than almost anyone else working  in television I mean it really is no  wonder how so the dragon's first season  had so much success the men and women  working behind the scenes were a  well-oiled machine firing on all  cylinders so you can imagine how Dev  devastated I was when I found out Miguel  was stepping down as one of its  showrunners before the first season had  even ended at first it didn't make sense  why he would want to walk away from a  major hit series I was actually shocked  when I heard this news although I  shouldn't have been because I did know  Miguel already had issues at HBO when he  was working under David and Dan now if  you remember back in August shortly  after House of the Dragon aired its  first episode we found out Miguel was  leaving the show that article stated  there's been a big shake up inside house  of the Dragon the HBO fantasy dramas  co-showrunner and director Miguel  sapochnik is stepping down from the hit  show they were basically saying Miguel  was leaving due to exhaustion from  working on House of the Dragon well  thanks to the new information that has  been released we now know that wasn't  the case there was some drama behind the  scenes at House of the Dragon involving  Miguel's wife who also worked on the  show now before I get into all of that  let me remind you of what girl said back  in August when he initially said he was  leaving the show he said working within  the Game of Thrones Universe for the  last few years has been an honor  especially spending the last two with  the amazing cast and crew of House of  the Dragon I am so proud of what we  accomplished in season one and Overjoyed  by the enthusiastic reaction of our  viewers it was incredibly tough to  decide to move on but I know that it was  the right choice for me as I do so  though I am deeply comforted to know  that Alan will be joining the series  he's someone I've known and respected  for a long time and I believe this  series could not be in safer hands I am  so glad to remain a part of the HBO and  House of the Dragon family and of course  I wish Ryan Condell and his team's  success in all the best was season 2 and  Beyond so as you can see there was no  real mention of why he was leaving  although another source said it was due  to exhaustion well now let me show you  what really happened behind the scenes  at the show in a stunning new article  released by Indie wire their headline  States Miguel left House of the Dragon  after HBO would not allow his wife to  serve as one of the show's producers now  all of you have actually seen his wife  before because she was an actress in  House of the dragon as well let me show  you what else was said and I will tell  you why I actually side with HBO  although I am a massive fan of Miguel's  work no show on television has more  family drama than House of the Dragon  HBO's soap opera about the Game of  Thrones Targaryen Clan fighting for  control of Westeros and that drama  apparently isn't just on screen  according to new reports about The  showrunners of the hit series shortly  after the first season aired back in  August co-showrunner Miguel sapochnick  announced he was leaving the show though  he would continue to Executive produce  the series HBO and Miguel framed his  exit as the amicable one however  according to the new information  Miguel's exit was far from Amico Bowl  the new information says that his leave  from the show was instead motivated by  disagreements with him and HBO over his  wife Alexis Rabin and her involvement in  House of the Dragon his wife Alexis was  in four episodes of the series as Talia  a lady in waiting to Allison Hightower  and she is credited as a producer on  season one of the show it looks like  Miguel was then again asking for his  wife to be included on the producing  team for the show's second season only  for HBO to refuse they did this because  of her inexperience her only producing  credit is on season 1 of the series you  can actually see that on her IMDb now  the article also says that HBO had to  bring in a mediator to de-escalate the  situation because things got so heated  Miguel ultimately decided to leave the  show over the disagreement firing his  agents at WME before going to the Rival  agency CAA with his wife so not only did  Miguel and his wife step down from House  of the Dragon but they also also fired  their agents and joined forces with  their Rivals obviously things must have  been very ugly behind the scenes  especially for Miguel to want to walk  away from such an incredible opportunity  the reason why HBO did not want to hire  his wife is because she did not have the  experience Miguel was basically wanting  her to be given that role simply because  she was his wife I must say I do agree  with HBO on this one they are learning  from their mistakes we already saw what  happened with David and Dan after they  no longer had George RR Martin's novels  to follow their inexperience became a  major issue for the show Once they no  longer had anything else to fall back on  I don't blame HBO for standing their  ground now I don't think Miguel's wife  would have had a major effect on the  show either way since she wasn't a  writer or director but I still don't  think she should have been given that  job over someone else who knows what  they're doing and I would say the same  thing if the genders were reversed for  example I think Lena Headey was one of  the greatest actor in Game of Thrones  and I would not want her husband  standing around messing up scenes just  because of his association with his wife  HBO did decline to comment on the story  to Indy wire now before joining season 1  of House of the dragon as co-showrunner  alongside Creator Ryan Condell who will  now serve as the sole showrunner of the  series Miguel directed six episodes of  Game of Thrones starting in season 5. on  House of the Dragon he directed the  first and the seventh episode drift Mark  in a story with The Hollywood Reporter  before the series aired Ryan Condell  admitted that Miguel was hesitant to  join House of the Dragon telling him I'm  never doing Game of Thrones again this  was all because of the issues he already  had while working under David and Dan so  we were actually lucky to have him on  House of the dragon at all now with that  being said I guess if one of the  showrunners did have to leave I would  rather it be Miguel although I do think  he is an amazing director I think they  are a lot easier to find than someone  like Ryan condo the reason why I believe  Ryan is so valuable to House of the  Dragon is because he's the one who  actually knows George RR Martin's story  he has at least read it and studied it  far more than David and Dan ever did I  would argue either way it is unfortunate  that Miguel did have to step down I do  respect him for standing beside his wife  but I also don't blame HBO for standing  their ground either it just sucks that  things had to get so messy we may never  see Miguel direct another episode in the  Game of Thrones Universe again now I  know him and kid Harrington are really  great friends so maybe he could convince  him to direct an episode of Jon Snow's  show if it ever gets made but outside of  that I don't see Miguel directing  anything else relating to Game of  Thrones at least we now know the real  reason why he wanted to leave the show  let me know what all of you think about  this leave me some of your thoughts down  below now for those of you who don't  know I am giving away the First full  season of House of the dragon all you  have to do to enter is make sure you're  subscribed I wanted to announce the  winner in my next video which would have  been this one but since it hasn't even  been 24 hours since I made that  announcement I will wait until I release  another one that way more of you are  aware of it so good luck and thank you  for showing Love by watching and  interacting with my videos I hope all of  you have a great day I will see you  again very soon  bye  [Music]  [Music]  foreign

